---
import Layout from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Layout title="Methodology — High Signal Podcasts">
  <h1>Methodology</h1>
  <p>
    High Signal Podcasts indexes public statements as claims. A published row always has a
    speaker, a verbatim excerpt that exists in the stored transcript segment, a date, and a
    source timestamp when YouTube captions exist.
  </p>
  <p>
    Daily GitHub Actions discover new episodes, take publisher or YouTube captions, skip
    filler with a cheap filter, and send only rec/stack (or claim) segments to the free-ai
    gateway. The website is server-rendered from the API, so new published claims appear
    without a rebuild.
  </p>
  <p>Missing evidence is shown as missing. We do not invent an answer.</p>
</Layout>
